"Command: Take Item": {
  "index": 4,
  "category": "constructs",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Command: Take Item"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "This command will cause the construct to "
        },
        {
          "text": "take an item out of the specified inventory",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ". \n\nThe "
        },
        {
          "text": "Rune of Marking",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " specifies the "
        },
        {
          "text": "side and position",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": " of the container to search. \n\n"
        },
        {
          "text": "The filter is optional",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and will take any item if left blank. \n\nIt requires the construct have "
        },
        {
          "text": "at least one grabber arm or storage torso",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": " to hold the item, and it can't already have something in it.  Stack merging is done as part of taking, but not during the initial check for performance reasons. As such, this command requires at least one empty slot somewhere in the construct's inventory. \n\nIf you give a construct two hands and want to fill both or wish to fill several inventory slots, you will need to use this command multiple times in a row."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}